Choosing a web designer in Cardiff isn't just about finding someone who can build a website. It's about finding someone who understands what you need your website to actually do — and has the track record to prove they can deliver it.

Cardiff has no shortage of web designers, agencies, and freelancers offering their services. That makes it harder, not easier, to pick the right one. Here's a straightforward guide to making the right choice for your business.

## Start with the outcome, not the process

Before you look at a single portfolio, get clear on what you need your website to achieve. Do you want to generate more enquiries? Rank higher on Google? Sell products online? Look more credible to potential clients?

The answer to that question should shape every conversation you have with a web designer. A good designer will ask about your goals early. One who jumps straight into talking about features, platforms, and timelines without understanding your business first is a red flag.

## Check their portfolio — and look past the visuals

A portfolio tells you a lot, but not everything. It's easy to make a website look good in a screenshot. What you actually need to know is whether those websites work.

When you look at a Cardiff web designer's portfolio, ask:

- Do the sites load quickly on mobile?
- Are the calls to action clear — is it obvious what the visitor is supposed to do?
- Do the sites rank on Google for relevant local searches?
- Are there real businesses in the portfolio, or just concept projects?

If a designer can show you a website for a Cardiff plumber or a local tradesperson that's generating enquiries from Google, that's far more valuable than a visually impressive site for a hypothetical brand.

[View the NC Digital portfolio](/portfolio/) to see real websites built for South Wales businesses.

## Ask whether SEO is built in from the start

A beautiful website that nobody can find is a waste of money. Local SEO — getting your site to appear in Google results when people in Cardiff search for your service — should be built into the foundation of every website, not bolted on as an afterthought.

Ask any Cardiff web designer you're considering:

- Do you include on-page SEO as standard?
- Will my site be set up correctly in Google Search Console?
- Do you offer ongoing SEO support?

At NC Digital, every [web design Cardiff](/web-design-cardiff/) project includes on-page SEO foundations as standard. If you want to go further after launch, our [Cardiff SEO service](/seo-cardiff/) can build on that foundation with a dedicated campaign.

## Understand who you're actually working with

Cardiff has a number of larger agencies that handle web design projects. On the surface, they look impressive — big offices, lots of staff, slick presentations. But when you sign up, you often end up working with a junior account manager who passes your brief down to a designer you'll never speak to.

If direct communication matters to you — if you want to talk to the person actually building your website — look for an independent designer or a small studio where that relationship is guaranteed.

## Watch out for these red flags

- **No portfolio** — if they can't show you examples of real work, walk away
- **Vague pricing** — "it depends" with no further detail usually means it'll cost more than you expect
- **No mention of SEO** — a designer who doesn't talk about search visibility isn't thinking about your long-term results
- **Templates dressed as custom work** — ask whether your site will be built from scratch or adapted from a purchased theme
- **No post-launch support** — once your site is live, you'll need help. Find out what's included after handover

## Ask about hosting and maintenance

Your website needs a home after it's built, and it needs regular care to stay secure and performing well. A good Cardiff web designer will offer — or at least be transparent about — [hosting and security](/services/website-hosting-security/), [maintenance packages](/services/website-maintenance-packages/), and what happens if something goes wrong.

If they hand over the site and disappear, you're on your own when the first problem arises.

## Consider whether you need branding too

If your logo looks amateur or you don't have consistent brand colours and fonts, a new website won't fix that — it'll just display your weak branding on a better-looking canvas. Some Cardiff web designers offer [logo design and branding](/logo-design-cardiff/) as part of their service, which means your identity and your website are designed together for a coherent result.

## The bottom line

The right Cardiff web designer for your business is one who:

- Asks the right questions about your goals before talking about features
- Has a real portfolio of working websites for businesses like yours
- Builds SEO in from the start
- Is clear about pricing, timelines, and what's included
- Stays available after launch

